Z||000019||88formula||12-31-2000||10:43 PM||||Well that depends on how tall you are. Knee deep for me is about 23"; knee deep for you may only be about 12" because you may be a short bastard.<P>Just kidding, I just hate snow whether it is 1"(inch) or 2'(feet). I hate it because I have to drive in it with a bunch of insane tailgating road raging drivers that usually hit me once every snow season and the salt ruins every part of the my vehicles. It costs me $8-$10 to get my truck cleaned every week and I have to shovel the stuff out of my huge four car driveway. Last year I got rear-ended once and side swiped a month later in my previous car that looks like Swiss cheese now from all the accidents it has been through. The year before that I got hit three times because of slippery conditions and drivers that don’t pay attention to the road. The year before the last year I got slammed in the side by some A-hole because he was trying to pass me on the only icy part of the road for 60 miles. It was a part that is always shaded by trees and the snow on the embankment was melting and freezing again on the shaded part. <P>Yesterday some guy decided to slam on his brakes coming towards me because he was going to fast around a corner and panicked. He started to slide sideways right for my New 2001 Toyota Tundra and almost hit me. If I had not turned off the road he would have surely hit me right if front of my house. I was on my way home from work. The sand that the MA highway department puts on the roads gets kicked up by traffic, which chips up your paint, especially the windshield. My old cars front-end looked like someone sand blasted it.<P>My brothers 87 fiero coupe you see in the first picture buried under the snow has been hit five times (fender benders) because of drivers that tailgate in slippery conditions, a real problem were I live. Four of the five times he was rear ended. The last one was just recently when an old lady was backing out of a bank. She backed right into my brother’s backside because there was snow on her back window and she could not see him. He was stuck in the parking lot behind a guy waiting for another diver to move from his space. <P>These are some of the reasons why I say snow s__ks and I hate winter.  <BR>||||reg||1
